  "raw_text": "225\n\nSol\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nSul\n\nSord\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsword\n \n/ espada\n\nSpirit\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nPirit\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nspirit, ghost\n \n/ espíritu, fantasma\n\nSpirit dukia walpa manakira pliki sakaia\n \n–\n \nDigging\n \nfor Spiritual Gems\n \n(part on Christian Life and Ministry\n\nmeeting)\n \n/ Busquemos perlas escondidas (parte de la reunión Vida y Ministerio Cristianos)\n\nSpirit holikira\n \n(a/t:\n \nSpirit hulikira\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nholy spirit\n \n/ espíritu santo\n\n(Construct:\n \nSpiritki\n \nholikira, Spiritkam holikira, Spiritka holikira\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n06/19\n):\n \nNahki upla kum sip sa G\nâ\nd spiritka holikira sarka paskaia?\n \n–\n \nHow can a person grieve God’s holy\n\nspirit?\n \n/ ¿Cómo puede una persona entristecer el espíritu santo de Dios?\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth\n-\n15\n):\n \nJehova ra makas spirit holikira maikbia\n \n–\n \nBeg Jehovah to give you holy spirit\n \n/ Ruega a Jehová que te dé\n\nespíritu santo\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb100\n):\n \nSpirit holikira ba Pal bara Timoti ra ani anira waia ba t\nâ\n \nbri kan\n \n–\n \nThe holy spirit was guiding\n \nPaul and\n\nTimothy wherever they went\n \n/ El espíritu santo guiaba a Pablo y a Timoteo donde quiera que fueran\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n03/20\n):\n \nDîa tânka sa ki Aisa nina ra, Luhpia nina ra bara spirit holikira nina ra tahbi daukaia ba, Matiu 28:19,\n\n20 aisi ba baku?\n \n–\n \nWhat does it mean to be baptized in the name of the Father, in the name of the Son, and in the name\n\nof the holy spirit, as it says at Matthew 28:19,20?\n \n/ ¿Qué significa ser bautizado en el nombre del Padre, en el nombre del\n\nHijo y en el nombre del espíritu santo, como se dice en Mateo 28:19,20?\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n11/21\n):\n \nJehova spiritka holikira ba hilp wan munisa diara nani dauki ba pain wabia dukiara.\n \n–\n \nJehovah’s holy\n\nspirit helps us so that what we are doing goes well (is successful).\n \n/ El espíritu santo de\n \nJehová nos ayuda para que lo que\n\nestamos haciendo salga bien (tenga éxito).\n)\n\nSpirit holikira tapahkanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nguidance of the holy spirit\n \n/ guía del espíritu santo\n\nSpirit Israel\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nspiritu\nal\n \nIsrael\n \n/ Israel espiritual\n\nSpirit lainka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nspiritual way\n, spiritually\n \n/\n \nde forma\n \nespiritual\n, espiritualmente\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n11/18\n):\n \nBan kra baha uplika ba kau isti spirit lainka ra p\nâ\nwbia\n \n–\n \nMaybe that person will grow in a spiritual\n\nway more\n \nquickly\n \n/ Tal vez esa persona crecerá de una manera espiritual más rápidamente\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n05/21\n):\n \nMaya waitna latwankira kum wîna tara lainka ra bara spirit lainka ra ai pamalika dîa nit ba yabia\n \n–\n \nA\n\nloving husband will give his\n \nfamily what they need physically and spiritually\n \n/ Un esposo amoroso le dará a su familia lo\n\nque necesitan física y espiritualmente\n)\n\nSpirit lainka ra pâwan\n \n–\n \nspiritually mature\n \n/ espiritualmente maduro\n\nSpirit lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nspirituality\n,\n \nspiritual way,\n \nspiritual\n \n/ espiritualidad,\n \nforma\n \nespiritual, espiritual\n\nSpirit lâka pawaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto grow spiritually\n \n/ crecer espiritualmente\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n02/19\n):\n \nspirit l\nâ\nka ra p\nâ\nwras sa\n \n–\n \nis not growing spiritually\n \n/ no está creciendo espiritualmente\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n10/20\n):\n \nSpirit l\nâ\nka ra pâwaia dukiara d\nî\na daukaia sip sa?\n \n–\n \nWhat can we do in order to grow in a\n\nspiritual way?\n \n/ ¿Qué podemos hacer para crecer en sentido espiritual?\n)\n\nSpirit lâka ra karna daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make strong in a spiritual way\n \n/ fortalecerse de una manera\nespiritual\n\nSpirit l\nâ\nka ra kauhla takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become cold spiritually, to become spiritually weak, to become\ninactive\n \n/ enfriarse espiritualmente, debilitarse espiritualmente, volverse inactivo\n\nSpirit l\nâ\nka ra kauhla takan muihni lakri nani\n \n–\n \nspiritually cold brothers and sisters, spiritually weak\nbrothers and sisters, inactive brothers and sisters\n \n/ hermanos y hermanas espiritualmente fríos,\nhermanos y hermanas espiritualmente débiles, hermanos y hermanas inactivos\n\nSpirit lâka tempelka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nspiritual temple\n \n/ templo espiritual\n\nSpirit mâ\n \n–\n \nfruitage of the spirit\n \n/ fruto del espíritu\n\nSpirit ni laikan Kristian\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nspirit-anointed Christian, Christian anointed with spirit\n \n/ cristiano ungido por\nespíritu, cristiano ungido con espíritu\n \n(a/t:\n \nBatana laikan kristian\n;\n \nBâk sakan uplika nani\n;\n \nBâk sakan\nkristianka nani\n;\n \nKristian batana laikan\n)\n\nSpirit pata\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nspiritual food\n \n/ comida espiritual\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-06/20\n):\n \nYawan karna trai munaia sa spirit pata ailal pali naiwa wanki ba wina yamnika sakaia dukiara\n \n–\n \nWe\nmust try hard in order to get the benefit(s) from the plentiful spiritual food being given to us today\n \n/ Debemos esforzarnos\nmucho para obtener los beneficios del abundante alimento espiritual que se nos da hoy)\n\nSpirit saura nani wal aisi uplika\n \n(\nsp\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nspirit medium\n \n/ médium espiritista\n\nSpirit saura warkka daukanka\n \n(\nsp\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nspiritism\n \n/ espiritismo\n\nSpirit uplika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nspirit person\n \n/ ser espiritual; persona de naturaleza espiritual; esp\ní\nritu",
